# What NetSurf may DO. Its namespace (nsemblink.ns) says what it may NAME.
#
# The same three classes Vellum gets, for the same reason: a browser runs
# whatever the network hands it, so it is the program on this machine that
# most needs to be unable to reach anything it was not given. No audio, no
# camera, no USB, no raw disk, no debug -- a bug in a foreign HTML parser
# cannot reach a device that was never granted.

filesystem     # the font, its own resources, local documents
network        # http and https over our own TCP and TLS
gpu            # a window is a GPU resource -- without this it cannot draw
